Use a relative base so the build works under a Pages project path

base: '/' assumed a custom domain at the domain root. On a GitHub Pages
project page the site is served from /<repo>/, so every absolute asset
URL resolved against the domain root and 404'd -- the deploy succeeded
and served a blank page.

base: './' works in both places, so attaching a custom domain later
needs no change. The two URLs built at runtime, the data fetch and the
portrait src, now go through import.meta.env.BASE_URL.

